> -rw-rw----    1 tang     games      113018 Jan 23 18:14 /var/games/nethack/save/9005tang.e.gz

That's an emergency save file that the game made for you when it realized
it was going to crash. All you need to do in this case is rename it to
9005tang.gz (in the same directory).

> From what I gathered from the man page, I ought to invoke 'recover' like so:

When you have an emergency save file, you don't need the recover utility.
You need it if the game crashes _without_ making an emergency save.
Then you'll probably have files called alock.0, alock.1 alock.2 and so on
in your playground directory, and alock is the base name for recover.
Happened to me once in August when we had a power failure here..

